# llm-gate judge credentials — copy this file to `.env` and fill in your key.
# `.env` is git-ignored; NEVER commit a real key.
#
# Judge metrics (faithfulness, answer_relevance) call an LLM via litellm,
# which reads standard provider env vars. Use any one of these:
#
#   Groq (free tier, fast — recommended for trying llm-gate):
GROQ_API_KEY=your_groq_key_here
#
#   OpenAI:
# OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_key_here
#
#   Google Gemini:
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_key_here
#
#   Local models (Ollama / LM Studio / vLLM / llama.cpp / LocalAI): NO key needed.
#   Set judge.model + judge.api_base in your suite YAML instead, e.g.:
#     judge:
#       model: ollama_chat/llama3.2
#       api_base: http://localhost:11434
#   or for any OpenAI-compatible local server:
#     judge:
#       model: openai/my-local-model
#       api_base: http://localhost:1234/v1
#
# The judge model is set in your suite.yaml (judge.model), e.g.
#   groq/openai/gpt-oss-120b
#   openai/gpt-4o-mini
#   gemini/gemini-2.0-flash
#   ollama_chat/llama3.2            (+ api_base)
